cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Hilbert's tenth problem in Lean"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 / mathlib development of the DPRM theorem and the
  computability-theoretic form of Hilbert's tenth problem. Semantic DPRM over
  the naturals — that a predicate on tuples of naturals is Diophantine exactly
  when it is recursively enumerable — is proved, together with the
  RE-completeness and undecidability of solvability for a finitely encoded
  polynomial, over the naturals and over the integers. The two formulations
  are shown many-one equivalent, by the substitution x = u - v in one
  direction and Lagrange's four-square theorem in the other, so Hilbert's own
  question about integer solutions is covered.
authors:
